      "content": "\"It is clear to anyone of sense that the Indian princely states, while possessing admirable traditions, lack the requisite administrative rigor for modern governance. The benevolent hand of the Crown is thus necessary to bring order, infrastructure, and efficient jurisprudence to these vast territories. We do not seek dominion for vanity, but to civilize and uplift a populace often prone to internal discord and questionable governance.\"",
